  "description": "Change of use of the dwelling (Use Class C3) to a children's care home for up to 2 child residents aged 7-18 (Use Class C2) with 24 hour care provided and carers working on a rota basis",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "1.&nbsp;The proposed development would result&nbsp;in the loss of a family-sized dwellinghouse, the need for which is clearly demonstrated in the Development Plan and supporting evidence base. Furthermore, the applicant fails to accurately demonstrate that there&nbsp;is an identified need for the children&#39;s home and the type of care proposed,&nbsp;which&nbsp;would not meet the current needs of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham (LBBD) Children’s Social Care, as confirmed by&nbsp;LBBD&#39;s Lead Commissioner in Children&#39;s Social Care. As such, the proposal is considered to have a detrimental impact on the borough&#39;s supply of family housing, would fail to meet local need and is therefore contrary to the following policies:&nbsp;National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (MHCLG, December 2024) Policy&nbsp;D7, H1, H12 and S2 of the London Plan (March 2021) Policies SP3 and&nbsp;SPDG1 of the LBBD Local Plan&nbsp; (September 2024)"
  ],
